# Test layers and file placement

## Colocation

Tests live **next to the code under test** — never in a distant mirror tree:

- `*.test.ts` — TypeScript only, no JSX.
- `*.test.tsx` — may import React.
- `*.integration.test.tsx` — composite module exercised with many mocked boundaries.

## Layers

| Layer | What it proves | Where |
|---|---|---|
| **Unit (pure)** | One module/function with controlled I/O; zero or few mocks | Colocated `*.test.ts` |
| **Store** | Zustand actions and state transitions; HTTP/storage/sibling stores mocked | `<Domain>.test.ts` |
| **Module integration** | Real internal orchestration with faked boundaries | `*.integration.test.tsx` |
| **Smoke** | Component renders with expected roles/`testID`s; heavy children mocked | `*.test.tsx` |

E2E (Detox / Maestro) is a separate concern; unit-level rules only require stable
kebab-case `testID`s as future E2E hooks.

## Unit test definition

One module or function, controlled inputs and outputs, no app boot, zero or minimal mocks.
This is the default layer — most business value lives in rules modules tested here.

## Integration test definition

Real orchestration between internal parts, with external boundaries faked (React Native
APIs, navigation, stores, assets). Use the `*.integration.test.tsx` naming when many
`jest.mock` calls target one composite behavior.

## Store tests

- Access state via `useStore.getState()`; reset state in `beforeEach`.
- Mock the HTTP client, sibling stores, mappers, and storage at module level.
- Assert **state transitions and action return values** — not pure logic, which belongs in
  the colocated `*Rules.test.ts`.

## Storybook's role

Storybook covers visuals and interactive harnesses. It is **never** a substitute for Jest
on rules, stores, or pure helpers.
